<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">El Hadj Umar Tall</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1797–<a href="/years/1864">1864</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Al-Hajj Umar Tall</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">El Hadj Umar Tall was a West African Muslim scholar and military leader of the nineteenth century who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toucouleur">Toucouleur</a> state through conquests in the 1850s and 1860s. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> identify him among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> leaders who drew inspiration from Sokoto's example.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…movements it inspired or encouraged reshaped governance across a broad arc of the Sahel and savannah: Seku Amadu's Massina Jihad (1818) and <b>Al-Hajj Umar Tall</b>'s Tukulor conquests (1850s–1860s) both drew on the Sokoto example, making dan Fodio's movement the foundational event of nineteenth-century West African Islamic political thought.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Weakened by factional rivalry, Futa Toro supplied many followers to <b>Umar Tall</b>, himself a native of the region.</blockquote><a href="/state/imamate-of-futa-toro">Imamate of Futa Toro</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 1850s Bundu was caught between <b>Umar Tall</b> and the French.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-bundu">Kingdom of Bundu</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1854 <b>Umar Tall</b> conquered Kaarta and killed its king Mamadi Kandia.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-kaarta">Kingdom of Kaarta</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Umar Tall</b> besieged it in 1857, but Paul Holl and Sambala held out until Faidherbe arrived.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-khasso">Kingdom of Khasso</a></li><li><blockquote>Rivalry with <b>Umar Tall</b>, a Tijani rather than a Qadiri, led to war.</blockquote><a href="/state/massina-empire">Massina Empire</a></li></ul></section>
